cff-version: 1.2.0

type: software
title: "Kidney PBPK Model — Furosemide & Protein-Bound Uremic Toxins"
abstract: >-
  A physiologically based pharmacokinetic (PBPK) model of the human kidney,
  representing competitive inhibition of OAT1/OAT3-mediated renal clearance
  of protein-bound uremic toxins (indoxyl sulfate, hippuric acid, p-cresyl
  sulfate) by furosemide, in healthy and CKD-5 physiology. Includes a
  142-state distributed tubular ODE system, parameter sensitivity analyses,
  and validation against published literature and clinical data.
authors:
  - given-names: Dr. Leyla Noroozbabaee
    affiliation: "MERLN Institute / cBITE / MaCSBio, Maastricht University"
keywords:
  - PBPK
  - pharmacokinetics
  - kidney
  - chronic kidney disease
  - uremic toxins
  - furosemide
  - OAT1
  - OAT3
  - drug-drug interaction
  - systems biology
